In goldenland-realestate-v2, the issue-tracker workflow is a user preference — missing it gets called out: keep a clean working tree, run the full test suite, commit with a clear message, then close the ticket via `gh issue close` with a summary comment, append a context pointer (e.g., the map's 'Implementation Decisions' section) to the parent issue, and commit the review ledger. The code-review skill reviews uncommitted work against a fixed point (HEAD for uncommitted changes) with the originating issue as spec source; findings go in `docs/agents/reviews/<issue-number>.md`. `.pi-subagents/` is pi-generated noise and must be gitignored. <!-- created=2026-08-06, last=2026-08-07 -->
